[Music]  in may a rare case of monkey box a virus  closely related to smallpox was  diagnosed in the uk that first uk case  which was from a traveler in nigeria is  now thought to be unconnected to the  wider outbreak but the uk went on quite  quickly to report many more cases today  the uk has the globe's highest monkey  pox case numbers and the viruses spread  to more than 4 500 confirmed or  suspected cases across at least 40  countries including the u.s and canada  on tuesday the cdc said they are  significantly expanding monkey pox  vaccination efforts in the u.s the  agency also said it is now recommending  vaccines for people with presumed  exposure to viral illness and not just  confirmed exposure so how serious is the  monkey pox outbreak and should americans  be concerned about contracting this  virus  last month world health organization  officials said they expected monkey pox  cases to grow but stressed the situation  was containable  this is a containable situation  particularly in the countries like where  we are seeing these outbreaks that are  happening across europe  in  north america as well this month the who  said that monkey pox doesn't at this  point constitute a global health  emergency they have said however that  they might revisit that decision  if the situation  worsens so for example if there was  evidence that people were getting more  severe disease or if there was evidence  that the virus was spreading into more  vulnerable groups like children or  people with weakened immune systems  in the u.s so far over 300 cases have  been confirmed across at least 27 states  and the district of columbia  textbook monkeybox uh typically starts  with flu-like symptoms you've got a  fever headache muscle like backache and  then a few days later you get a rash uh  normally starting on the face and  spreading out and it's a little like  chickenpox so it starts as these  flat red marks they get become kind of  pimple like but in the current outbreak  there have been lots of case reports of  pretty different looking symptoms some  people are getting no rash some people  are getting  very subtle rashes a lot of times people  are noticing a concentration of the rash  in the genital area rather than starting  in the face  scientists believe the main way  monkeyprox is spread is by close contact  previous research found that monkeypox  virus particles spread over short  distances via respiratory droplets but  it is unknown whether monkey pox can  spread by tinier airborne particles  known as aerosols so there are high  levels of virus in the like the  pus-filled lesions that the disease  causes and contact with that is thought  to be the main mode of spread monkey  pulse is much less easily spread than a  virus that can be spread easily through  the air like covered 19 would be an  obvious example um but if you are in  very close contact with someone then it  is quite easy to catch u.s health  officials found that monkey pox cases  are concentrated in specific communities  according to the cdc at least some of  the u.s cases were people who identify  as gay bisexual or men who have sex with  men the virus can impact anyone  regardless of sexuality but infectious  disease experts think that the virus is  exploiting very close contact between  some members of this community to spread  this is the first time since the hiv  epidemic of the 1980s that a newly  emerging disease has you know cropped up  and is  concentrated in this community um  one big difference between now and then  is that while public health authorities  were very slow to respond to the hiv  epidemic this time they are making a lot  of effort to get the message out to gay  and bisexual men and they're doing  things like handing out information at  pride events they're sending push  notifications on dating apps like grindr  most cases of monkeypox resolve on their  own without treatment however there are  some antiviral drugs and a vaccine that  were developed for smallpox that also  work against monkeypox  on tuesday danish vaccine maker bavaria  nordic which is the only producer of a  vaccine licensed for monkey pox said it  will meet demand it's just like a  traditional vaccine it it builds your  immune system it stimulates your immune  system so you are better prepared to  fight the  monkey parks  you are infected with monkey pox was  discovered in lab monkeys in denmark in  1958 hence the monkey in monkey pox that  said monkeys aren't thought to be the  main vector or carrier of the disease  scientists aren't totally sure what  species is the main carrier but it seems  to be very widely circulating among  certain rodents in the rainforests  of the congo basin in central africa  and the first human case was  discovered in 1970 in a nine-year-old  boy in the democratic republic of congo  in the current outbreak about four and a  half thousand people have been confirmed  with monkeypox in countries where the  virus doesn't normally occur and none of  those have died thus far there's only  been one death in nigeria  [Music]

